{"id": "EUVD-2026-103617", "enisaUuid": "277fc52e-8152-3a27-b7db-edd3cbbc31d8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Fix immediate JMP JEQ/JNE on MIPS32\n\nAn addu instruction was emitted instead of addiu, causing the immediate\nvalue 1 to be interpreted as register $at. This made the comparison\nresult invalid when the immediate operand was negative. Note that $at\nis mapped to BPF_REG_AX, which is used for constant blinding.\n\nFix the instruction to use the immediate form.\n\nFound with test_bpf on MIPS32r1 emulated by QEMU.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1547e9f3a7d71971216e6dba30270cae13fe4e02", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/beeae92e70e705e90a0d6d9b3b8498ee3b92f495", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6f939529ed6c580e9b6c5daa20be67fa0b3d4cf0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/876ef04c75c2751acfd355606fca3eced71dec65", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1bd91670966a7142ac94f2cebe2b5ae6bf5cb0c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db762fd96be225bd06161c9631160c755d891693"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jqhp-gcf3-75rx", "CVE-2026-98572"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2c191bf6-d9f1-34f1-a572-2d4b0ae525bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "3cafdc74-b78b-36cf-9e00-ce8d4f0ebdee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb63cfcd2ee8ec3805f6881f43341f589c3d2278 <db762fd96be225bd06161c9631160c755d891693"}, {"id": "508c5f34-37f8-3a67-951c-c0e5109d9e78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb63cfcd2ee8ec3805f6881f43341f589c3d2278 <beeae92e70e705e90a0d6d9b3b8498ee3b92f495"}, {"id": "721c061d-c9ed-35a3-968a-b7571aefe8a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7f78791a-a67c-380b-